  <modelingNote rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This separates *Nummulitoides* especially from fully involute *Ranikothalia*.</modelingNote>
  <modelingNote rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">massive marginal cord + quasi-/subevolute adult coiling</modelingNote>
  <bestDifferentiatingObservation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The most useful combination is:</bestDifferentiatingObservation>
  <sectionNote rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Where this distinction is critical, both axial and equatorial information may be needed; the literature specifically warns that these early nummulitid genera can be misidentified when only one section orientation is available.</sectionNote>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

