  <rdfs:label rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Chordoperculinoides</rdfs:label>
  <modelingNote rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">involute test + massive marginal cord + coarse vertical canals</modelingNote>
  <modelingNote rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Chordoperculinoides* differs especially from *Nummulitoides* because the latter becomes quasi-/subevolute, whereas *Chordoperculinoides* remains involute.</modelingNote>
  <bestDifferentiatingObservation rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The strongest diagnostic combination is:</bestDifferentiatingObservation>
  <sectionNote rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Reliable separation from *Ranikothalia* and *Nummulitoides* may require axial as well as equatorial information; diagnosis should not be forced from a single unsuitable random section.</sectionNote>
</owl:NamedIndividual>

